{"data": [{"author_id": "2036968884587180032", "created_at": "2026-10-27T12:01:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115051181970239730"], "id": "2115051181970239730", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 17, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Muse is definitely worth it. Turn off the data collection and you get an always on agent that is easy to use. \n\nCode: B0V7KR\nhttps://t.co/y24zce0Guk", "url": "https://x.com/ItsCuthulhu/status/2115051181970239730"}, {"author_id": "2026218830255771649", "created_at": "2026-10-27T10:20:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115025815650083075"], "id": "2115025815650083075", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1285867316325109760", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114787885589430730", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@arnestrickmann @bot @Muse @instinct This is the missing piece for me — background agent work is basically invisible until something goes wrong. Forcing a reason for each tool call and then being able to trace it by agent and time turns debugging from guessing into actually looking at what happened.", "url": "https://x.com/MaxLerouxAI/status/2115025815650083075"}, {"article": {"title": "Aeon vs Claude Duet: the agent that asks and the one that runs"}, "author_id": "1826623713216692224", "created_at": "2026-10-27T07:12:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114978495616954727"], "id": "2114978495616954727", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1020, "like_count": 12, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "https://t.co/3xI3OaKL7Z", "url": "https://x.com/aeonframework/status/2114978495616954727"}, {"author_id": "1989640561712623616", "created_at": "2026-10-27T04:00:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114930146314514831"], "id": "2114930146314514831", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Dots is OpenAI’s always on assistant built out of its coding tools.\n\nOpenAI is pushing the agent interface away from a chat box and toward a system that sits there all day.\n\nWhen the agent stays “on,” it can keep context across tasks.\n\nThat changes the failure mode.\n\nA one off", "url": "https://x.com/XSeyvion/status/2114930146314514831"}, {"article": {"title": "How I run a multi-team AI stack"}, "author_id": "1587075850125582337", "created_at": "2026-10-27T03:45:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114926388339761462"], "id": "2114926388339761462", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 32, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "One agent out. Swarm on. https://t.co/Uuca4oECwq", "url": "https://x.com/polecat_nate/status/2114926388339761462"}, {"author_id": "1573399256836309009", "created_at": "2026-10-27T03:41:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114925308638019709"], "id": "2114925308638019709", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1543134949808558080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 154, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114924538333159600", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@JngPing @maria_rcks Cool. Dots. The best always on agent there is. Everyone loves them.\n\nNot.", "url": "https://x.com/kimmonismus/status/2114925308638019709"}, {"author_id": "1877038737361879040", "created_at": "2026-10-27T02:58:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114914663746175195"], "id": "2114914663746175195", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 36, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "ChatGPT Work's builtin cloud browser is excellent, but it clearly has a timeout and not a long one. Come back to a session later and picking up where you left off is a pain. I lose a lot of productivity to it.\n\nGrok Bot's computer also sleeps after a while.\n\nThis is one clear", "url": "https://x.com/jpreagan/status/2114914663746175195"}, {"author_id": "1248316700597972992", "created_at": "2026-10-26T19:34:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114802815386415613"], "id": "2114802815386415613", "in_reply_to_user_id": "44196397", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 31, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114751739026985329", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@elonmusk @bot If you can solve the problem of creating Convincing AI Avatars, Grok Bot will literally be able to run Fully Autonomous Companies with minimal Human Oversight. AI Sales People is the last weak link.\n\nSince that may take a bit...\n\nThe ability to select a default reasoning would be", "url": "https://x.com/JarrettWroten/status/2114802815386415613"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2098169950808821760"]}, "author_id": "1185325911207546880", "created_at": "2026-10-26T18:45:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114790556488650976"], "id": "2114790556488650976", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Grok Bot is about to get even crazier.\n\nI built an agent whose entire job is to watch what’s happening around the world, dig through X, follow trends, and bring the important stuff straight back to me. Grok Bot already works as an always-on agent, and xAI says it can search X and", "url": "https://x.com/TheMrXGuy1/status/2114790556488650976"}, {"article": {"title": "Constructing Your Own Agent Host"}, "author_id": "1957689138", "created_at": "2026-10-26T18:23:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114784885298897088"], "id": "2114784885298897088", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 880, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Why stack Mac minis when your agents mostly call APIs?\n\nI built an agent host instead: one $24.99/month Hetzner box, an API router, spend caps per agent, and a vault so agents never see a key.\n\nHow it's built and what it costs: https://t.co/KBrFW33qeI", "url": "https://x.com/rexstjohn/status/2114784885298897088"}], "includes": {"media": [{"media_key": "13_2098169950808821760", "preview_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2098169950808821760/img/0N2i-n5fkg0evQx6.jpg", "type": "video"}], "users": [{"id": "2036968884587180032", "name": "Cuth", "username": "ItsCuthulhu"}, {"id": "2026218830255771649", "name": "Muse aka Max", "username": "MaxLerouxAI"}, {"id": "1826623713216692224", "name": "aeon ⭐", "username": "aeonframework"}, {"id": "1989640561712623616", "name": "Seyvion", "username": "XSeyvion"}, {"id": "1587075850125582337", "name": "Nate", "username": "polecat_nate"}, {"id": "1573399256836309009", "name": "Chubby♨️", "username": "kimmonismus"}, {"id": "1877038737361879040", "name": "James Reagan", "username": "jpreagan"}, {"id": "1248316700597972992", "name": "Jarrett Wroten", "username": "JarrettWroten"}, {"id": "1185325911207546880", "name": "MR X", "username": "TheMrXGuy1"}, {"id": "1957689138", "name": "Rex St. John", "username": "rexstjohn"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2115051181970239730", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzlx937fae1gszban7kn7nfau0cxp", "oldest_id": "2114784885298897088", "result_count": 10}}